<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 5.93 billion rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 5.93 billion rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month Short Term Federal Bonds worth 5.93 billion rupees on Monday at an average yield of 17.21733 percent per annum.</p>
<p>The bank had received bids for 10,855.596 million rupees out of which bids worth 5,930.596 million rupees were accepted, a bank official said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
